Subject: Debugging on Windows via WSL
Message-ID: <ZXwm3fS3rzA.pfftm3e7DQAJ@tmb-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/tmb-users/c/ZXwm3fS3rzA/m/pfftm3e7DQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

Running gdbsource() under Windows has been notoriously unstable across different
versions of R/gcc. I was therefore happy to find out that

https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Subsystem_for_Linux

lets you install linux under Windows, and that gdbsource() works smoothly (at
least under my current installation).

There are a a few steps involved in setting up WSL, which should be
written down step-by-step, but I thought I would let people know
right away that this is a possible route to debugging under Windows.

